cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived data, please cite the manuscript below and the underlying data sources."
title: "Pre-Injury Hepatic Transcriptome Predicts Later-Onset Drug-Induced Liver Injury in Rat: Compound-Held-Out Evidence Beyond Dose"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a forward-prediction study of drug-induced liver
  injury in rat. Compound-dose arms that are histopathologically normal at day 4 are used
  to predict confirmed injury at day 15 or 29, under leave-one-compound-out validation and
  against an administered-dose baseline. All confidence intervals resample whole compounds
  rather than individual arms.
